What can be the reason if a server is taking more time after reboot? 

If our server is suddenly taking significantly longer to reboot, it is usually caused by pending OS updates, stuck startup services, or hardware initialization processes 

1.The server may be applying patches or cumulative updates, which can substantially delay the boot process. 

2.A specific startup application, database (e.g., SQL Server), or network service might be timing out. 

3.Servers perform exhaustive hardware and memory checks on a hard boot, which takes longer if we have a massive amount of RAM. 

4.Dead SAN-Storage Area Network /NAS Network Attached Storage mounts (unresponsive drives) or network drives waiting to reconnect will cause long boot delays. 

5.If the server did not shut down cleanly, the OS may be running a time-consuming disk consistency 

